."] [216 3 "// blocked: pending when kill returns, as the kernel makes it (queue 231: sigpending right after saw nothing, the"] [217 3 "// signal still on its way through Go's handler thread)"] [227 1 "// the interval timers (ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL, ITIMER_PROF), counted in wall time"] [241 1 "// setItimer arms which's timer (value 0 disarms), returning the old value and interval."] [260 3 "// disarmed: an expiry not yet handled is dropped, as the kernel's single pending bit is taken by the"] [261 3 "// handler that disarms it"] [282 5 "// a Python handler: delivered here, under the timer's lock, so a disarmed timer sends no more"] [283 5 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches it)"] [312 2 "// the start installs SIGINT's handler (py-os-1124; pylifecycle's init_signals, _PySignal_Init: a program that never"] [313 2 "// imports signal ends with KeyboardInterrupt at a SIGINT, not by the signal; test_subprocess's test_send_signal)"] [334 4 "// as at CPython's start: SIGINT's default_int_handler, SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored, the rest SIG_DFL"] [340 4 "// a SIGHUP ignored at the process's start (nohup, a parent's SIG_IGN): SIG_IGN, as CPython's signal_get_set_handlers"] [341 4 "// reads it (py-mods-1122)"] [346 4 "// SIGINT's default_int_handler, unless the process started with SIGINT ignored (signal_install_handlers sets it"] [347 4 "// only over SIG_DFL: a child of nohup or of a SIG_IGN keeps ignoring it)"] [467 5 "// the C handler runs inside raise(): the Python handler before raise_signal returns"] [490 4 "// set_wakeup_fd(fd, /, *, warn_on_full_buffer=True)"] [599 5 "// only the main thread runs handlers: wait for any arrival"] [603 4 "// until a signal is pending (a stale wake-up token is not one)"] [656 7 "// delivered on unblocking: the default action or nothing"] [715 5 "// the own process's signal (a pidfd of another process times out here, harmlessly) handled"] [716 5 "// before the call returns, as the kernel delivers it"]] :go/pos